<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Washington is a 58-year-old head of government with complete edentulism, who comes for his yearly preventive visit two weeks after his new complete dentures were delivered. Two days ago he had one adjustment for a sore spot under the lower denture, which is already less tender. He rates his chewing 6 out of 10, up from 3, and has added minced meat, fish and cooked vegetables to his diet; he takes the nutritional supplement once a day. His speech was lisping for the first few days and is now nearly normal when he reads aloud. Two lower implants are planned in one week. He has had no tetanus booster for more than ten years, has never had a pneumococcal or zoster vaccine, and has never had a colon cancer screening test. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 58</td></tr><tr><td>Dentures</td><td>New complete dentures for two weeks; one adjustment; chewing 6 of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>93.6 kg, up 1.2 kg since intake</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-2 0</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Acetaminophen as needed (none this week); oral nutritional supplement once a day</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on paper in the waiting room and reviewed with him by Dr. Pritchard-Boateng. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Demanding work he finds meaningful; married, raising two grandchildren; feels supported</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>One or two glasses of wine with dinner on most days; AUDIT-C 3 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Rides or walks most days for 45 to 60 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Diet widening with the new dentures; protein at each meal; supplement once a day</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven hours; rises early</td></tr><tr><td>Safety at home</td><td>Feels safe; firearms stored locked and unloaded</td></tr><tr><td>Road safety</td><td>Wears a seat belt; does not drive himself</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Reading glasses; no hearing difficulty</td></tr><tr><td>Oral health</td><td>Under prosthodontic care; implants planned</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

