<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated. Lipid panel: total cholesterol 196, HDL 48, LDL 124 and triglycerides 120 mg/dL. With blood pressure 122/76, no smoking and no diabetes, his 10-year atherosclerotic risk by the pooled cohort equations is about 7%, below the 10% at which a statin is recommended for primary prevention; tooth loss is associated with cardiovascular disease in cohort studies, but the association is not proven to be causal and does not change the estimate. [S]<list><item>No statin; repeat lipids in five years or sooner if risk changes.</item><item>Colorectal cancer screening with a stool immunochemical test (FIT) kit today, colonoscopy as the alternative.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Complete edentulism with new complete dentures (K08.103)</content>. New dentures are stable after one adjustment, with a sore spot healing; chewing and diet are improving; implant surgery is planned next week. [S]<list><item>Continue denture care as taught.</item><item>Implant surgery as planned by prosthodontics.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Unintended weight loss with nutritional risk (R63.4)</content>. Weight up 1.2 kg since intake as the diet widens. [S]<list><item>Continue the supplement once a day until chewing is fully restored.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>122/76 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid screening and cardiovascular risk</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Total cholesterol 196, HDL 48, LDL 124, triglycerides 120 mg/dL; 10-year risk about 7%; statin not indicated; tooth loss noted as an association only</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Hemoglobin A1c 5.4% at intake; BMI 26.5</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Age 45 to 75; FIT kit given today</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Declined</td><td>Benefits and harms of a PSA test discussed at 58; he chose not to be tested this year and will revisit it next year</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Once for all adults; drawn today with his agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Once for all adults; drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Triple panel once for all adults; drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Up to date</td><td>AUDIT-C 3 at intake, below the threshold for men</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Oral health and oral cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Under prosthodontic care; mucosa examined today: a healing sore spot only</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tdap given today; last booster more than ten years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 single dose today; recommended for all adults aged 50 and older</td></tr><tr><td>Zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First recombinant zoster dose today; second in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Received this season in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Discussed under shared clinical decision-making; he will decide with the autumn vaccines</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tdap vaccine; last tetanus booster more than ten years ago; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine (PCV20), single dose, recommended for all adults aged 50 and older; Recombinant zoster vaccine, first of two doses [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Periodontal disease and atherosclerotic vascular disease: does the evidence support an independent association? A scientific statement from the American Heart Association (2012); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Statin Use for the Primary Prevention of Cardiovascular Disease in Adults: Preventive Medication (2022); Colorectal Cancer: Screening (2021); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026); Expanded Recommendations for Use of Pneumococcal Conjugate Vaccines Among Adults Aged ≥50 Years: Recommendations of the Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices — United States, 2024 (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Implant surgery with prosthodontics next week. Twelve-week review in four weeks. FIT kit returned by mail. HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B results at the next visit. Second zoster dose in two to six months. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-04-13: twelve-week review: new complete dentures six weeks in use, three weeks after two lower implants were placed; eating, speech, weight and healing. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.21" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 20 minutes, with his consent, before his implant surgery. He named a health care agent, a long-time friend, and a health care proxy form was completed; the agent is recorded in the chart and is not named here. He said that what matters most to him is a clear mind, his independence and finishing the work he has begun, and that he would want a trial of full treatment for a sudden illness, including breathing support, if recovery were likely. The plan will be revisited yearly or after any serious illness. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>
